# Setting up


npm init -y 
npm install express
npm install -D nodemon
npm install mongoose
npm install -D dotenv
npm install mocha chai --save-dev


The server.js is the entry point of the API
set "dev": "nodemon server.js"
"test":"mocha"

[npm run test || npm test] for running unit test.

mocha runs the test and chia is for the 

Change the commonjs type to module, as we can write code in python sytle

.env file is to be created for keeping the credentials 

mocha: is the test runner of the test file (Engine running the test)
chai: provided required syntax and behaviour as expected (Gear box, stearing, break)

## Understanding the Package.json file 

The basic informations are in key value pair JSON format. 
The dependencies which are only used during the development of the project are kept in dev dependencies. 
The script are run for set task, like for testing mocha and chai are set. For dev/ running the server dev is kept.
The remaining dependencies which are required for the API are kept inside the dependencies key. 

### Understanding the version of dependencies installed 

version: (symbol) 4.1.3
here, 4 is the major version 
.1 is the minor version 
.3 is the patch version 

^  accepts minor and patch version updates but not the major version change. 
~  accepts only the patch version change not the minor version. 
none  no symbols means the exact version is required. 
* wild card or means any version, or x. 

## Folder structure 

MVC architecture is being followed for the project 

Model, View and Controller

Model: Will have the actual schema of each Object which is going to be stored in the DB
View: Here View is not used as we are later using React for the Front end. 
Controller: This will Handle the actual logic/ business logic of the code. 

There are others as well. 

Middleware: These are for recurshive checking of some logic, like is this user logged in or not in every page. 
Routes: Routes are for linking the URL to the controllers for handling the logic. 
Error middlesware: A type of middleware for checking error in each page, making the error logs more reusable. 
config: Connection to external dependencies like database, or other services like OAuth and so on. 
unitls: For utilities code like password hashing, checking password, permission checking. 
tests: used for mocha and chai for unit testing files 
.env: Inside the root directory, for keeping the sepcret keys like API and JWT token and all. 

